Well, if there are any other physicists out there, feel free to correct me.
The SC theory means that while the cat is in the box, we have no way of 
knowing the state, whether it's dead or alive.  Dead and Alive are what we
perceive to be two separate states with totally separate wave functions.
However, in the box, this is not so.  The wave function of the cat in the box
is a linear combination of the two wavefunctions. 

NOW HERE's THE POINT>

The wave packet doesn't collapse.

When we open the box, we perturb the wave function and force it into one
of the states.  The cat is either dead or alive depending on when we open the
box...  Of course, the wavefunction might not be symmetric, and be highly
biased to the dead side...  but I would tend to agree that there is a 50/50
possibility that the cat could be alive when you open the box.


